From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:14:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bytecompiler: drop each compiled scope's name lookup map

A finished code block resolves every name by index, so the scopes it owns no longer need
their lookup maps; boa_ast rebuilds one if a direct eval asks. The realm's scope keeps its
map, since every later script compiles against it.
---
 src/bytecompiler/mod.rs | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/bytecompiler/mod.rs b/src/bytecompiler/mod.rs
index 3d51ec9..1a70597 100644
--- a/src/bytecompiler/mod.rs
+++ b/src/bytecompiler/mod.rs
@@ -2811,6 +2811,16 @@ impl<'ctx> ByteCompiler<'ctx> {

         let source_map_entries = self.source_map_builder.build(final_bytecode_len.as_u32());

+        // Kitesurf: names resolved to indices by now, and a later direct eval rebuilds the map
+        // it needs. The realm's scope stays mapped, since every script compiles against it.
+        for constant in &self.constants {
+            if let Constant::Scope(scope) = constant {
+                if !scope.is_global() {
+                    scope.ks_drop_lookup();
+                }
+            }
+        }
+
         CodeBlock {
             length: self.length,
             register_count,
